  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="32">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 32</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gyf þeowman æt þam ordale fúl weorðe, mearcie man hine æt þam forman cyrre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-a">And gif þeofman æt þam ordale ful weorðe, mearcyge man hine æt þam forman cerre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-q">Si seruus in ordalio reus fuerit, signetur prima uice.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="32" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ gyf þeo[w]man æt ðam ordale ful wurðe, mearcie [man] hine ðonne æt ðam forman cyrre.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gyf þeowman æt þam ordale ful weorðe, mearcie man hine æt þam forman cyrre.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And if a slave is found guilty at the ordeal, he shall be branded on the first occasion.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And if a slave is proven guilty by ordeal, the first time he is to be branded.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And if a slave is convicted by the ordeal, on the first occasion he is to be branded.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wenn ein Unfreier (Dieb B A?) beim Ordal schuldig befunden wird, so werde er (dann B) beim ersten Mal gebrandmarkt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if a slave (thief, B A?) is found guilty at the ordeal, let him (then, B) be branded the first time.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="336"><ref target="clause:IAtr_2">I Atr 2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 2</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_2">I Atr 2–2.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 32-32:1: I Atr 2-2:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="367"><label>echoes</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_1-5">I Atr 1.5</ref> <quote>I Atr 1:5, 2, 4 (echoed by II Cn 30:3b,4, 32, 33)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="367"><label>echoes</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_2">I Atr 2</ref> <quote>I Atr 1:5, 2, 4 (echoed by II Cn 30:3b,4, 32, 33)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="367"><label>echoes</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_4">I Atr 4</ref> <quote>I Atr 1:5, 2, 4 (echoed by II Cn 30:3b,4, 32, 33)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="467"><label>source</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_2">I Atr 2</ref> <quote>From here until 33.2, the source is still I Ethelred (2, 2.1, 4–4.3).</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="467"><label>source</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_2-1">I Atr 2.1</ref> <quote>From here until 33.2, the source is still I Ethelred (2, 2.1, 4–4.3).</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="467"><label>source</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_4">I Atr 4–4.3</ref> <quote>From here until 33.2, the source is still I Ethelred (2, 2.1, 4–4.3).</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">B and A's ‘þeofman’ (thief) is perhaps an error of the archetype. Liebermann compares I Atr 2.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">From here until 33.2, the source is still I Ethelred (2, 2.1, 4–4.3). I Ethelred 3, which deals with security and witness at sales, is omitted, presumably because it breaks the sequence of ideas. With 4.3. I Ethelred comes to an end.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">The Harley and Corpus texts have wrongly “a thief”.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þeowman: ðeofman AB</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">man: omitted B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">hine: hine þonne B</note>
      </div>
